        "# cFish.io WordPress Development Standard Operating Procedures (SOP)\r",
        "\r",
        "This document outlines the standard procedures for common development tasks for cFish.io WordPress site.\r",
        "\r",
        "## Table of Contents\r",
        "\r",
        "1. [Development Environment Setup](#development-environment-setup)\r",
        "2. [Feature Development Workflow](#feature-development-workflow)\r",
        "3. [WordPress.com Admin Workflow](#wordpresscom-admin-workflow)\r",
        "4. [GitHub-WordPress.com Integration](#github-wordpresscom-integration)\r",
        "5. [Content Updates](#content-updates)\r",
        "6. [Theme Customization](#theme-customization)\r",
        "7. [Plugin Management](#plugin-management)\r",
        "8. [WordPress Core Updates](#wordpress-core-updates)\r",
        "9. [Database Management](#database-management)\r",
        "10. [Deployment Procedures](#deployment-procedures)\r",
        "11. [WordPress Studio Usage (Limited)](#wordpress-studio-usage-limited)\r",
        "12. [Troubleshooting Common Issues](#troubleshooting-common-issues)\r",
        "13. [Platform Integration](#platform-integration)\r",
        "\r",
        "## Development Environment Setup\r",
        "\r",
        "### Initial Setup\r",
        "\r",
        "1. **Clone the repository**\r",
        "   ```\r",
        "   git clone https://github.com/cFischi/cFish.git\r",
        "   cd cFish\r",
        "   ```\r",
        "\r",
        "2. **Set up Git credentials**\r",
        "   ```\r",
        "   git config --global user.name \"Your Name\"\r",
        "   git config --global user.email \"your.email@example.com\"\r",
        "   git config --global credential.helper wincred\r",
        "   ```\r",
        "\r",
        "3. **Create local WordPress configuration**\r",
        "   - Create a `wp-config.php` file (this is not in version control)\r",
        "   - Configure database connection parameters\r",
        "   - Set up debug mode for development\r",
        "\r",
        "### Environment Synchronization (Modified Workflow)\r",
        "\r",
        "1. **Primary Development: WordPress.com Backend**\r",
        "   - Most development and content updates happen directly on wordpress.com\r",
        "   - Use draft/preview mode for testing changes\r",
        "   - Export theme modifications as needed for version control\r",
        "\r",
        "2. **Code Version Control: Cursor & GitHub**\r",
        "   - Major code changes developed in Cursor\r",
        "   - Backed up and versioned in GitHub\r",
        "   - Used for collaborative development and tracking changes\r",
        "\r",
        "3. **WordPress Studio (Limited Usage)**\r",
        "   - Used mainly for offline development and WP-CLI operations\r",
        "   - Not a primary part of daily workflow\r",
        "\r",
        "## Feature Development Workflow\r",
        "\r",
        "1. **Create a feature branch**\r",
        "   ```\r",
        "   git checkout -b feature/descriptive-name\r",
        "   ```\r",
        "\r",
        "2. **Development Approach Options**\r",
        "   \r",
        "   **Option A: WordPress.com Direct (Preferred)**\r",
        "   - For minor to moderate changes\r",
        "   - Make changes directly in WordPress.com Customizer or editor\r",
        "   - Test in draft/preview mode\r",
        "   - Document changes for later backup to version control\r",
        "\r",
        "   **Option B: Local Development & Upload**\r",
        "   - For complex changes requiring offline work\r",
        "   - Make code changes in Cursor\r",
        "   - Commit to feature branch\r",
        "   - Upload to WordPress.com for testing\r",
        "   - Document results\r",
        "\r",
        "3. **Commit changes incrementally**\r",
        "   ```\r",
        "   git add .\r",
        "   git commit -m \"Descriptive message about changes\"\r",
        "   ```\r",
        "\r",
        "4. **Push changes to GitHub**\r",
        "   ```\r",
        "   git push -u origin feature/descriptive-name\r",
        "   ```\r",
        "\r",
        "5. **Test on WordPress.com**\r",
        "   - Upload changed files to WordPress.com if needed\r",
        "   - Test in draft/preview mode\r",
        "   - Document test results\r",
        "\r",
        "6. **Create Pull Request**\r",
        "   - Go to GitHub repository\r",
        "   - Create PR from feature branch to main\r",
        "   - Document changes and testing performed\r",
        "\r",
        "7. **Review and Merge**\r",
        "   - Review code in GitHub\r",
        "   - Merge to main when approved\r",
        "   ```\r",
        "   git checkout main\r",
        "   git pull origin main\r",
        "   git merge feature/descriptive-name\r",
        "   git push origin main\r",
        "   ```\r",
        "\r",
        "## WordPress.com Admin Workflow\r",
        "\r",
        "### Safe Testing on WordPress.com\r",
        "\r",
        "1. **Using Draft Mode**\r",
        "   - Create draft posts/pages for testing content changes\r",
        "   - Preview drafts to see how they will appear when published\r",
        "   - Only publish when fully tested\r",
        "\r",
        "2. **Theme Customizer**\r",
        "   - Use the built-in Customizer for theme modifications\r",
        "   - Changes in Customizer are previewed before publishing\r",
        "   - Save changes only when satisfied with results\r",
        "\r",
        "3. **Plugin Testing**\r",
        "   - Test new plugins in isolation when possible\r",
        "   - Have a rollback plan before activating major plugins\r",
        "   - Document plugin test results\r",
        "\r",
        "4. **Backup Before Major Changes**\r",
        "   - Create a backup point before significant changes\r",
        "   - Use WordPress.com's built-in backup features or plugins\r",
        "   - Know how to restore from backup if needed\r",
        "\r",
        "## GitHub-WordPress.com Integration\r",
        "\r",
        "WordPress.com Business plan includes an official GitHub Deployments feature that provides native integration between your GitHub repository and WordPress.com site, enabling automated or manual deployments.\r",
        "\r",
        "### Setup and Configuration\r",
        "\r",
        "1. **Access GitHub Deployments**\r",
        "   - Go to your WordPress.com dashboard\r",
        "   - Navigate to Tools → GitHub Deployments\r",
        "   - Click \"Connect Repository\"\r",
        "\r",
        "2. **Repository Connection**\r",
        "   - Authenticate with your GitHub account when prompted\r",
        "   - Choose between:\r",
        "     - Connect an existing repository\r",
        "     - Create a new repository from your WordPress.com site\r",
        "   - Select the repository you want to connect\r",
        "   - Configure initial deployment settings\r",
        "\r",
        "3. **Deployment Configuration**\r",
        "   - Set branch to deploy from (e.g., `main`, `development`, or feature branches)\r",
        "   - Configure deployment triggers:\r",
        "     ```\r",
        "     Automatic: Deploy on every push to the selected branch\r",
        "     Manual: Only deploy when manually triggered from dashboard\r",
        "     ```\r",
        "   - Set file paths to include/exclude (if needed)\r",
        "   - Configure pre-deployment GitHub Actions workflows (optional)\r",
        "\r",
        "### Standard GitHub-to-WordPress.com Workflow\r",
        "\r",
        "1. **Code Development**\r",
        "   - Develop in Cursor IDE as usual\r",
        "   - Commit to feature branches\r",
        "   - Push to GitHub\r",
        "\r",
        "2. **Testing Approaches**\r",
        "   \r",
        "   **Approach A: Manual Testing (Recommended for Initial Tests)**\r",
        "   - Push changes to feature branch on GitHub\r",
        "   - Log into WordPress.com dashboard\r",
        "   - Navigate to Tools → GitHub Deployments\r",
        "   - Manually trigger deployment from feature branch\r",
        "   - Test changes on live or staging site\r",
        "   \r",
        "   **Approach B: Automated Testing**\r",
        "   - Configure automatic deployments for certain branches\r",
        "   - Push to designated testing branch\r",
        "   - Changes automatically deploy to WordPress.com\r",
        "   - Monitor deployment status in run logs\r",
        "   \r",
        "   **Approach C: Staging Site Testing**\r",
        "   - For Business plans with staging sites\r",
        "   - Configure GitHub deployments to update staging environment\r",
        "   - Test thoroughly before promoting to production\r",
        "\r",
        "3. **Deployment to Production**\r",
        "   - After successful testing, merge feature branch to main\r",
        "   - If automatic deployments are enabled, changes will deploy automatically\r",
        "   - If using manual deployments, trigger final deployment from dashboard\r",
        "   - Verify deployment in run logs\r",
        "   - Document changes in changelog\r",
        "\r",
        "4. **Monitoring Deployments**\r",
        "   - Check Tools → GitHub Deployments → Deployment Run Logs\r",
        "   - Review status of all deployments\r",
        "   - Troubleshoot any failed deployments\r",
        "   - Document deployment history\r",
        "\r",
        "### Maintaining Code Integrity\r",
        "\r",
        "1. **GitHub as Source of Truth**\r",
        "   - Always treat GitHub repository as the canonical source code\r",
        "   - Direct edits on WordPress.com should be avoided when possible\r",
        "   - If emergency changes are made directly on WordPress.com, commit those changes back to GitHub\r",
        "\r",
        "2. **Version Control Best Practices**\r",
        "   - Use semantic versioning for releases\r",
        "   - Tag significant releases in GitHub\r",
        "   - Maintain a detailed changelog\r",
        "   - Use descriptive commit messages\r",
        "\r",
        "3. **Backup Procedures**\r",
        "   - WordPress.com handles backups of the production site\r",
        "   - GitHub preserves code history and versions\r",
        "   - Consider additional backup solutions for critical projects\r",
        "\r",
        "### GitHub Actions Integration (Advanced)\r",
        "\r",
        "1. **Pre-Deployment Processing**\r",
        "   - Create GitHub Actions workflows for:\r",
        "     - Code linting and validation\r",
        "     - Asset compilation (Sass, JavaScript, etc.)\r",
        "     - Automated testing\r",
        "   - Configure these to run before deployment\r",
        "\r",
        "2. **Notification Workflows**\r",
        "   - Set up GitHub Actions to notify team of successful/failed deployments\r",
        "   - Integrate with Slack, email, or other notification systems\r",
        "\r",
        "## Content Updates\r",
        "\r",
        "### Blog Posts\r",
        "\r",
        "1. **Create/edit content in WordPress.com Editor**\r",
        "   - Use WordPress.com block editor for content creation\r",
        "   - Preview content before publishing\r",
        "   - Save as draft for team review if needed\r",
        "\r",
        "2. **Media Management**\r",
        "   - Optimize images before upload (compression, proper dimensions)\r",
        "   - Use descriptive filenames and alt text\r",
        "   - Organize media library with folders if using appropriate plugin\r",
        "\r",
        "### Page Updates\r",
        "\r",
        "1. **Major page structure changes**\r",
        "   - Create in draft mode first\r",
        "   - Preview extensively across devices\r",
        "   - Document changes in version control after publishing\r",
        "\r",
        "2. **Minor content updates**\r",
        "   - Make directly in WordPress.com editor\r",
        "   - Use preview mode to verify changes\r",
        "   - Document changes in change log\r",
        "\r",
        "## Theme Customization\r",
        "\r",
        "1. **Theme file modifications**\r",
        "   - For advanced customizations, use Cursor for code development\r",
        "   - Version changes in Git\r",
        "   - Upload to WordPress.com for testing\r",
        "   - Document implementation process\r",
        "\r",
        "2. **CSS Customizations**\r",
        "   - Preferably use WordPress.com's Additional CSS feature\r",
        "   - Test changes using preview\r",
        "   - For complex changes, develop in Cursor first\r",
        "   - Document CSS modifications\r",
        "\r",
        "3. **JavaScript Enhancements**\r",
        "   - Create separate JS files for custom functionality\r",
        "   - Test locally before uploading\r",
        "   - Verify compatibility across browsers\r",
        "\r",
        "## Plugin Management\r",
        "\r",
        "1. **Adding new plugins**\r",
        "   - Research plugin reputation, support, and compatibility\r",
        "   - Install in WordPress Studio test environment first\r",
        "   - Export/copy files to Cursor workspace\r",
        "   - Commit with detailed description of plugin purpose\r",
        "\r",
        "2. **Updating plugins**\r",
        "   - Test updates in staging environment first\r",
        "   - Document plugin version changes\r",
        "   - Create separate branch for significant plugin updates\r",
        "\r",
        "3. **Removing plugins**\r",
        "   - Verify dependencies before removal\r",
        "   - Clean up any orphaned data\r",
        "   - Document removal reason\r",
        "\r",
        "## WordPress Core Updates\r",
        "\r",
        "1. **Preparation**\r",
        "   - Full backup of site and database\r",
        "   - Document current WordPress version\r",
        "\r",
        "2. **Update process**\r",
        "   - Perform update in WordPress Studio first\r",
        "   - Test core functionality\r",
        "   - Copy updated files to Cursor workspace\r",
        "   - Commit with detailed update notes\r",
        "\r",
        "3. **Post-update checks**\r",
        "   - Verify all custom functionality still works\r",
        "   - Check theme compatibility\r",
        "   - Confirm plugin compatibility\r",
        "\r",
        "## Database Management\r",
        "\r",
        "1. **Local database updates**\r",
        "   - Document schema changes\r",
        "   - Consider migration scripts for significant changes\r",
        "\r",
        "2. **Database synchronization**\r",
        "   - Use WordPress export/import for moving content\r",
        "   - Replace URLs in database when moving environments\r",
        "   - Never directly edit production database\r",
        "\r",
        "## Deployment Procedures\r",
        "\r",
        "1. **Pre-deployment checklist**\r",
        "   - Code review completed\r",
        "   - All tests passing in wordpress.com preview mode\r",
        "   - Feature branch merged to main\r",
        "   - Documentation updated\r",
        "\r",
        "2. **Deployment**\r",
        "   - For changes developed locally: Upload to WordPress.com\r",
        "   - For changes made in WordPress.com: Publish from draft/preview\r",
        "   - Document deployment time and version\r",
        "\r",
        "3. **Post-deployment verification**\r",
        "   - Check critical site functionality\r",
        "   - Verify visual integrity across devices\r",
        "   - Confirm third-party integrations\r",
        "\r",
        "## WordPress Studio Usage (Limited)\r",
        "\r",
        "### Overview\r",
        "- WordPress Studio serves as a **secondary environment** for special cases\r",
        "- Refer to [wordpress-studio-guide.md](wordpress-studio-guide.md) for detailed capabilities and limitations\r",
        "- **Not recommended for primary development** due to performance and usability issues\r",
        "\r",
        "### When to Use Studio\r",
        "1. **Offline Development Needs**\r",
        "   - When internet access is limited or unreliable\r",
        "   - For experimenting with high-risk changes\r",
        "   - As a local backup environment\r",
        "\r",
        "2. **WP-CLI Operations**\r",
        "   - For database exports and manipulation\r",
        "   - Bulk content operations not available in WordPress.com\r",
        "   - Custom scripts requiring server access\r",
        "\r",
        "3. **File Synchronization (Infrequent)**\r",
        "   - Use synchronization batch files only when necessary\r",
        "   - Verify changes in WordPress admin after synchronization\r",
        "   - Consider this a fallback approach, not primary workflow\r",
        "\r",
        "## Troubleshooting Common Issues\r",
        "\r",
        "### Git Issues\r",
        "\r",
        "1. **Authentication failures**\r",
        "   - Verify GitHub credentials\r",
        "   - Check Windows credential manager\r",
        "   - Reset/update stored credentials if needed\r",
        "\r",
        "2. **Merge conflicts**\r",
        "   - Identify conflicting files\r",
        "   - Resolve conflicts with appropriate merging strategy\r",
        "   - Test thoroughly after conflict resolution\r",
        "\r",
        "### WordPress Issues\r",
        "\r",
        "1. **White screen of death**\r",
        "   - Check PHP error logs\r",
        "   - Disable plugins one by one\r",
        "   - Revert to default theme temporarily\r",
        "\r",
        "2. **Database connection errors**\r",
        "   - Verify database credentials in wp-config.php\r",
        "   - Check database server is running\r",
        "   - Confirm database user permissions\r",
        "\r",
        "3. **Plugin conflicts**\r",
        "   - Disable all plugins then enable one by one\r",
        "   - Check for JavaScript errors in browser console\r",
        "   - Verify theme compatibility with plugins\r",
        "\r",
        "## Platform Integration\r",
        "\r",
        "### Core Platform Overview\r",
        "Our integrated system leverages four key platforms for comprehensive business operations:\r",
        "\r",
        "#### Platform Roles & Functions\r",
        "\r",
        "- **cFish.io - WordPress (Content Management)**\r",
        "  - Handle customer-facing content deployment\r",
        "  - Manage landing pages and product documentation\r",
        "  - Process initial client inquiries\r",
        "\r",
        "- **cFish.App - ClickUp (Task Management Hub)**\r",
        "  - Track project progress with automated status updates\r",
        "  - Manage development sprints and team workflows\r",
        "  - Generate performance metrics and reports\r",
        "\r",
        "- **U.cFish.io - Notion (Knowledge Center)**\r",
        "  - Maintain comprehensive documentation and SOPs\r",
        "  - Create and store project templates\r",
        "  - Enable real-time collaborative editing\r",
        "\r",
        "- **cFish.Vip - Vendasta (Client Solutions)**\r",
        "  - Track service delivery and client interactions\r",
        "  - Manage CRM and sales pipeline\r",
        "  - Monitor client project status\r",
        "\r",
        "#### Documentation Hierarchy\r",
        "- U.cFish.io (Notion) for comprehensive documentation\r",
        "- cFish.App (ClickUp) for active project management\r",
        "- cFish.io (WordPress) for client-facing content\r",
        "\r",
        "### Unified Workflow Process\r",
        "\r",
        "- **Project Lifecycle**\r",
        "  - Initial client contact via WordPress forms\r",
        "  - Project planning in ClickUp with Notion documentation\r",
        "  - Service delivery through Vendasta\r",
        "  - Continuous documentation updates in Notion\r",
        "  - Continuous projects and communications in ClickUp\r",
        "\r",
        "### Daily Operations Schedule\r",
        "\r",
        "- Morning: Sync WordPress and Vendasta dashboards\r",
        "- Midday: Update ClickUp tasks and Notion documentation\r",
        "- Evening: Cross-platform status review\r",
        "\r",
        "### Communication Protocols\r",
        "\r",
        "- Internal: ClickUp for tasks, Notion for knowledge sharing\r",
        "- External: WordPress forms for inquiries, Vendasta for service updates\r",
        "\r",
        "### Review & Reporting Cycle\r",
        "\r",
        "- Weekly: ClickUp progress tracking and WordPress content updates\r",
        "- Monthly: Vendasta service metrics review"
      ]
    }
